{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler","id":936817,"title":"Fate spoiler!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-24T17:28:24-07:00","id":936817,"title":"Fate spoiler!","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-bindings-of-fate/\" target=\"_blank\">Apparently, it's a fanfic author.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> It takes what was already there, invents its own story about them, and when shipping, it has all the subtlety of Venus herself appearing on a heart-shaped bed at the edge of a lake screaming &quot;KISS! KIIISSSS!!!&quot; through a megaphone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T18:19:10-07:00","id":936830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler#post936817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-bindings-of-fate/\" target=\"_blank\">Apparently, it's a fanfic author.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> It takes what was already there, invents its own story about them, and when shipping, it has all the subtlety of Venus herself appearing on a heart-shaped bed at the edge of a lake screaming &quot;KISS! KIIISSSS!!!&quot; through a megaphone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It was my impression that we are role players. Who here hasn't written fan fiction in their lives? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T19:44:36-07:00","id":936860,"title":"","content":"Here's a thought; Fate conspires to give Scions servants and lovers, but almost as universal in myth as those two archetypes? Rivals.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying, a Scion of Tyr should mind their fingers around stray dogs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T05:57:35-07:00","id":937024,"title":"","content":"SO then, Fate doesn't force you to do anything. It just <i>encourages</i> you to do what it wants.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, maybe the Aesir don't have to die, after all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T07:59:09-07:00","id":937093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler?p=937024#post937024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case, maybe the Aesir don't have to die, after all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they still have to die.<br /> <br /> This is Fate on the Origins and Hero level. It starts getting teeth at Demigod, and for Gods it's downright...well, binding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 07-25-2016, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:33:11-07:00","id":937219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler#post936817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-bindings-of-fate/\" target=\"_blank\">Apparently, it's a fanfic author.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> It takes what was already there, invents its own story about them, and when shipping, it has all the subtlety of Venus herself appearing on a heart-shaped bed at the edge of a lake screaming &quot;KISS! KIIISSSS!!!&quot; through a megaphone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always imagined Fate was three old ladies watching their Soap Operas and cackling over the misfortune of others (while also shipping and swooning over great drama and grand tales).<br /> <br /> I also get constant flashbacks to Ed Harris from <b>The Truman Show.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 07-25-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T12:34:50-07:00","id":937220,"title":"","content":"I think it's important to note that Fate doesn't force *you* to do anything. Fate tracks down someone who's already inclined to do what Fate wants done, and then provides the opportunity. If the Aesir have to die, Fate doesn't grab a rando off the street. Fate finds someone who already hates the pantheon and has an appropriate skill set; then Fate arranges for that person to learn what's required to take the Aesir down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T15:10:40-07:00","id":937323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagardner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler?p=937220#post937220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's important to note that Fate doesn't force *you* to do anything. Fate tracks down someone who's already inclined to do what Fate wants done, and then provides the opportunity. If the Aesir have to die, Fate doesn't grab a rando off the street. Fate finds someone who already hates the pantheon and has an appropriate skill set; then Fate arranges for that person to learn what's required to take the Aesir down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, that's probably the most exciting thing to me.<br /> <br /> Fate is fundamentally the Fatebound's <i>mentor. </i>If a Nemesis is selected, Fate will make it so that opportunities to remain a threat to the person they hate will keep on falling into their lap. If a Boon Companion is selected, Fate will ensure they are never irrelevant to their friend.<br /> <br /> You have no idea how many story issues this solves right there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T17:42:02-07:00","id":937385,"title":"","content":"It's amazing how one little shift can change the whole context. I never really used Fatebinding in the 1E games I ran, but the whole &quot;Fate finds someone who can fill the role and nudges them in the right direction&quot; is so much more appealing to me. As many mentioned, it's more palatable if, say, rather than pointing at a random mortal and saying &quot;You! You're in love!&quot;, instead Fate says &quot;You! The one who's had a crush on the Scion for months! I'm gonna have his car break down, and you'll be there to let him use your phone!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T20:26:33-07:00","id":937430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler?p=937093#post937093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, they still have to die.<br /> <br /> This is Fate on the Origins and Hero level. It starts getting teeth at Demigod, and for Gods it's downright...well, binding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could lets say a Scion of Thor dodge the whole Ragnarok fate by opting to join a new or different pantheon, and shunning the Aesir?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T21:04:51-07:00","id":937455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler?p=937430#post937430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could lets say a Scion of Thor dodge the whole Ragnarok fate by opting to join a new or different pantheon, and shunning the Aesir?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sure the Vanir would like to think so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmmm, now there's an idea. Maybe while their parents are getting slaughtered, the children of the Aesir reassemble their pantheon under a different name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T22:55:05-07:00","id":937490,"title":"","content":"Conceptually I love Fate in-setting, though there is a nagging oddness to the fact that Fate makes life more story-shaped, but our chronicles are already prone to being more story-shaped by virtue of being roleplaying chronicles. So In some ways Fate in just an in-setting explanation for what would already likely be the course of events? At least at the Origins/Hero level before it starts growing more coercive teeth at the Demigod level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T00:06:39-07:00","id":937498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler?p=937490#post937490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conceptually I love Fate in-setting, though there is a nagging oddness to the fact that Fate makes life more story-shaped, but our chronicles are already prone to being more story-shaped by virtue of being roleplaying chronicles. So In some ways Fate in just an in-setting explanation for what would already likely be the course of events? At least at the Origins/Hero level before it starts growing more coercive teeth at the Demigod level?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just an explanation, it's a tool. Having the mechanic and the list of possible things that can happen can inspire the Director, and help her pin down what would be the most interesting thing to happen at that given stage or with a given character.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hm, a Fatebinding. Say, didn't you say that you might be interested in having a sidekick? Well congratulations! Boon Companion. Have fun with your little buddy!&quot;<br /> <br /> Speaking for myself, I <i>know</i> that if I ever took the Director's chair I would want all the help that I could get, and the Fate mechanics sound like the sort of thing I would be <i>extremely</i> grateful for. Even if it's only reminding me that these sorts of things <i>happen at all</i> 3 hours deep into a game after a week of work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T07:02:41-07:00","id":937579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler?p=937219#post937219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also get constant flashbacks to Ed Harris from <b>The Truman Show.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Cue the sun</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T07:16:31-07:00","id":937583,"title":"","content":"So what happens if you try to break a Fatebinding now that it doesn't have overt control over your actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T11:03:03-07:00","id":937688,"title":"","content":"If you don't want Ragnarok in your chronicle, then don't use it, mythology be damned. I treated it as propaganda that another enemy started just to throw the Aesir off their game, and it made a pretty good plotline. It's your story - do what you like with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T12:54:38-07:00","id":937729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler?p=937579#post937579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Cue the sun</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>do do do do...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T12:57:20-07:00","id":937730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/936817-fate-spoiler?p=937583#post937583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens if you try to break a Fatebinding now that it doesn't have overt control over your actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>But think about the peppy cute girl who's had a crush on you for months who just now got a chance to have Scion-pai notice her! You'll break her heart!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T18:48:24-07:00","id":937862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>